<title>USA: Mellon Bank seen as takeover target - report.</title>
<headline>Mellon Bank seen as takeover target - report.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mellon Bank Corp is seen as takeover by companies such as NationsBank, Chase Manhattan Corp, First Union Corp, Northern Trust and Bank of New York, Business Week reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>One shareholder told the magazine, &quot;The talking point in terms of price is $55 a share.&quot;</p>
<p>Fueling the buyout speculation is the lack of a successor for Mellon's chief executive, Frank Cahouet, and slow growth in its retail and corporate banking units, the magazine reported.</p>
<p>Mellon and potential suitors declined to comment to the magazine.</p>
</text>
